68
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:48,240
So basically your car runs on gasoline.

69
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:52,060
So you put your key into the ignition and you turn it.

70
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:57,360
This in turn sends energy to this little motor called the starter motor.

71
00:03:57,920 --> 00:04:05,220
And that basically gets the car going by means of an electrical current before the gasoline ignites.

72
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:16,300
So it's like a little electrical motor that makes the spark plug ignite and causes some of the mechanical parts like the pistons move within the car and then it turns on.

73
00:04:16,520 --> 00:04:16,640
Okay.

74
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:20,900
